Subject: [PATCH] Report version before device detection
Upstream: not submitted

The CLI constructs every subcommand before argparse handles --version. That
initializes EngineArgs and fails device inference for a ROCm package on hosts
without a visible GPU. Handle the standalone version flags before importing
backend-specific subcommands.

diff -Naur a/vllm/entrypoints/cli/main.py b/vllm/entrypoints/cli/main.py
--- a/vllm/entrypoints/cli/main.py	2026-08-21 03:31:54.881768225 +0800
+++ b/vllm/entrypoints/cli/main.py	2026-08-21 03:32:00.738270017 +0800
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@
 
 
 def main():
+    # Version reporting must not initialize backend-specific subcommands.  In
+    # particular, a ROCm package may be queried on a host without a GPU device.
+    if len(sys.argv) == 2 and sys.argv[1] in ("-v", "--version"):
+        print(importlib.metadata.version("vllm"))
+        return
+
     import vllm.entrypoints.cli.benchmark.main
     import vllm.entrypoints.cli.collect_env
     import vllm.entrypoints.cli.launch
